1
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,316
When a shopper contacts an online fashion store,

2
00:00:06,316 --> 00:00:08,111
the question may sound simple.

3
00:00:08,111 --> 00:00:10,256
Is this available in my size?

4
00:00:10,256 --> 00:00:12,260
How should I care for the fabric?

5
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:14,005
Can you help me check an order?

6
00:00:14,005 --> 00:00:17,344
But behind each question is a real workflow.

7
00:00:17,344 --> 00:00:19,836
Someone needs to understand the request,

8
00:00:19,836 --> 00:00:21,604
find accurate information,

9
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:23,339
decide what can be answered,

10
00:00:23,339 --> 00:00:26,070
and recognize when a team member should take over.

11
00:00:26,070 --> 00:00:30,186
That's where a thoughtful AI support experience becomes valuable.

12
00:00:33,686 --> 00:00:35,671
With GRINDCTRL’s Store Chat,

13
00:00:35,671 --> 00:00:39,523
shoppers can ask questions directly inside a Shopify store.

14
00:00:39,523 --> 00:00:42,927
The assistant works from the store knowledge the merchant provides,

15
00:00:42,927 --> 00:00:45,115
including information about products,

16
00:00:45,115 --> 00:00:47,384
sizing, delivery, and care.

17
00:00:47,384 --> 00:00:51,004
And support doesn't have to stop when a question gets complicated.

18
00:00:54,504 --> 00:00:56,362
If the shopper needs a person,

19
00:00:56,362 --> 00:00:58,996
the conversation can be handed to the merchant’s team,

20
00:00:58,996 --> 00:01:01,265
together with the reason for the handoff.

21
00:01:01,265 --> 00:01:04,741
The team can review the conversation in a shared inbox,

22
00:01:04,741 --> 00:01:05,596
assign it,

23
00:01:05,596 --> 00:01:06,904
add private notes,

24
00:01:06,904 --> 00:01:09,602
and respond with saved replies when appropriate.

25
00:01:09,602 --> 00:01:13,275
The goal isn't to make every conversation sound automated.

26
00:01:13,275 --> 00:01:17,788
It's to keep context and make the transition from AI to human support

27
00:01:17,788 --> 00:01:18,568
feel organized.

28
00:01:22,562 --> 00:01:25,862
Some workflows can also work with order information.

29
00:01:25,862 --> 00:01:29,590
Where access is configured and the shopper's details are verified,

30
00:01:29,590 --> 00:01:33,274
the assistant can look up order status on a read-only basis.

31
00:01:33,274 --> 00:01:35,069
It does not change orders,

32
00:01:35,069 --> 00:01:38,802
issue refunds, or make decisions beyond its approved scope.

33
00:01:42,302 --> 00:01:44,148
For the people running the store,

34
00:01:44,148 --> 00:01:49,614
this means customer conversations and support actions can be easier to
follow in one place.

35
00:01:49,614 --> 00:01:55,661
The experience can be adapted to the merchant's actual policies, rather
than relying on generic answers.

36
00:01:55,661 --> 00:01:58,186
And the same principle applies to setup.

37
00:01:58,186 --> 00:02:01,502
The right configuration depends on the store's catalog,

38
00:02:01,502 --> 00:02:03,353
theme, support process,

39
00:02:03,353 --> 00:02:05,905
and the questions customers ask most often.

40
00:02:09,405 --> 00:02:11,011
To see what this looks like,

41
00:02:11,011 --> 00:02:13,506
open the GRINDCTRL Demonstration Store.

42
00:02:13,506 --> 00:02:17,588
You can explore the shopper experience and discuss the setup with the
team.

43
00:02:17,588 --> 00:02:18,903
GRINDCTRL

44
00:02:18,903 --> 00:02:23,400
AI that helps the store respond and knows when people should take over.
